  "description": "RILZER crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P c a 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C12 H42 Cr2 Nd3 O27 3+,Na1 1+,4(Br1 1-),8(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Cr2 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.493-4.162 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.39-112.80°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Cr2Nd3(μ-OOCCH3)6(μ-OH)6(H2O)9]Br3·NaBr·8H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 9 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
